Expose $modsecurity_intervention and $modsecurity_triggered_rules.

Backport of owasp-modsecurity/ModSecurity-nginx pull request #374 ("Add
modsecurity log vars", module part) to v1.0.4. The rule ids come from
msc_get_rules_messages_rule_ids(), added to libmodsecurity in v3.0.17, so no
log message is parsed and nothing about the request is written anywhere:
the edge layer reads both variables in its log phase.

  $modsecurity_intervention      "1" once ModSecurity made a disruptive
                                 intervention (deny, redirect), else "0"
  $modsecurity_triggered_rules   comma-separated ids of the rules that
                                 matched and were logged, in match order

